{
 "translation": "That is what they call a heart of comfort and a heart of iron. We played together, grew up together, went to school together, and then college. But to this insensitive lump of flesh... Ugh! My blood boiled again. Be quiet, merciless one! I wish that instead of a human, God had made you a rock, on which I couldn't even find a meaningful word. Your indifference doesn't hurt others. Just think, what wrong did innocent Kishwar do to you? What pain did she cause you? She, who is more innocent than a little bird. She, who has bowed her head and endured the world's sorrows, and is still enduring them. She, whom her cruel mother is sacrificing for wealth and fame. She, who is going with her head bowed, willingly, towards the sacrificial altar.",
